The target is the conjunction of the three frozen simplifier obligations. I’ll instantiate the hooked symbols with Lean’s integer/Boolean operations, define Python-style modulo as the frozen `((x % y) + y) % y`, and define the odd-digit product by a terminating decimal recursion on the nonnegative magnitude. This matches the K loop’s quotient, parity test, zero sentinel, and accumulator multiplication rather than baking in any target equality.
